  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nA non-VAT-registered seller cannot issue a VAT invoice. Under Section 236 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), only VAT-registered persons are authorized to issue VAT invoices. This is further supported by Revenue Regulations No. 16-2005, which defines a \"VAT-registered person\" as one who is registered as a VAT taxpayer under the provisions of the NIRC.\n\nIn practical terms, if a seller is not registered for VAT, they must issue a regular sales invoice instead, which does not include VAT. This distinction is crucial for compliance and proper documentation in business transactions.\n\n### Relevant Facts / Assumptions\nThe factual circumstances have not been fully described. The analysis is based on the question as presented.\n\n### Alternative Interpretations\nNo alternative interpretations identified from the available indexed authorities.\n\n### Position Strength\nPosition strength is preliminary and subject to full fact pattern verification.",
